Voting logic is the mechanism that compares the outputs from the redundant modules and decides the system's final output. In TMR, it typically implements a majority vote (2-out-of-3).
```
function vote_2_of_3(output_A, output_B, output_C):
    if output_A == output_B:
        return output_A
    else if output_A == output_C:
        return output_A
    else if output_B == output_C:
        return output_B
    else:
        // All three outputs are different. This indicates a more complex failure
        // or an unresolvable state, requiring specific error handling.
        return ERROR_NO_MAJORITY
```
